          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-2-core-concepts/data-warehousing/#star-snowflake-scd--surrogate-keys">Surrogate Keys</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Let us take one ex: Suppose 'XYZ' is customer in Bangalore, he was residing in the city from the last 5 years, in the period of 5 years he has made purchases worth of 3 lacs.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-2-core-concepts/data-warehousing/#star-snowflake-scd--surrogate-keys">SCD</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">What is Hybrid Slowly Changing Dimension? After we create a SCD Table can we use that Particular Dimension as a Dimension Table for Star Schema?</span></li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li class="rm-index-group">
        <h3 class="rm-index-heading"><a href="/level-2-core-concepts/data-warehousing/#facts-dimensions--measures">Facts, Dimensions &amp; Measures</a></h3>
        <p class="rm-index-desc">27 interview questions covering Dimensions, Relational Model, Dimensional Modeling, Fact Tables.</p>
        <ul class="rm-index-subs">
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-2-core-concepts/data-warehousing/#facts-dimensions--measures">Dimensions</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Conformed dimensions are the dimensions, which can be used across multiple Data Marts in combination with multiple facts tables accordingly.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-2-core-concepts/data-warehousing/#facts-dimensions--measures">Relational Model</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Differentiate between dimension and attribute?</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-2-core-concepts/data-warehousing/#facts-dimensions--measures">Dimensional Modeling</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">What are Fact and Dimension and Measure? Can a Dimension Table contain numeric values?</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-2-core-concepts/data-warehousing/#facts-dimensions--measures">Fact Tables</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Semi-Additive: Semi-additive facts are facts that can be summed up for some dimensions in the fact table, but not the others.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </li>
