          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-2-core-concepts/data-warehousing/#normalization--relational-theory">Normalization</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">Database normalization is a data design and organization process applied to data structures based on rules that help build relational databases.</span></li>
          <li><span class="rm-index-sub-label"><a href="/level-2-core-concepts/data-warehousing/#normalization--relational-theory">Relational Theory</a></span> <span class="rm-index-sub-desc">The tuple-oriented calculus uses a tuple variables i.e., variable whose only permitted values are tuples of that relation.</span></li>
